# Data conversion between kibibyte and kilobyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kibibyte and kilobyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KiB to 1.024KB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 1.536KB; backward, converting 1KB to 0.9765KiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 1.4648KiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(forward_whole->to(KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(forward_fractional->to(KB))
backward_whole: int = 1KB
print(backward_whole->to(KiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_fractional->to(KiB))

<<< stdout
1.024KB
1.536KB
0.9765KiB
1.4648KiB

<<< stderr
